==English==

===Etymology===
From {{af|en|profuse|-ly|id2=adverbial}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|en|/pɹəˈfjusli/|a=US}}
* {{audio|en|en-us-profusely.ogg|a=US}}

===Adverb===
{{en-adv}}

# In great [[quantity]] or [[abundance]]; in a [[profuse]] manner.
#: {{ux|en|The run left him sweating '''profusely'''.}}
#* {{RQ:Doyle Land of Mist|passage="Oh, I say! By Jove! What!" was his oration, after which he resumed his seat and perspired '''profusely'''.}}
#* {{quote-book |en |title=A Key to the Eucalypts: With Descriptions of 522 Species and 150 Varieties |author={{w|William Blakely|William Faris Blakely}} |year=1965 |publisher=Forestry and Timber Bureau |isbn=0642950776 |page=180 |text=A shrubby species suitable for beefarming, as it flowers '''profusely''' from November-January, and yields both pollen and nectar.}}

